WEBVTT

00:00.440 --> 00:01.720
Wait until Your Majesty

00:01.800 --> 00:03.720
Hands over Xie Xuan, then he'll come

00:03.800 --> 00:05.760
By then no one can fault him

00:05.840 --> 00:07.240
Enough

00:10.240 --> 00:11.640
Order Zhu Yuanzhi

00:12.280 --> 00:13.680
To rescue the emperor

00:13.880 --> 00:15.280
Yes

00:17.500 --> 00:22.500
You waited bitterly for many days, yet Zhu Yuanzhi delayed under various pretexts, leaving his grand army motionless.

00:23.000 --> 00:29.500
Zu Yue received urgent dispatches stating that Wunu had taken a detour to ambush Zhu Yuanzhi's army; with the defense line in jeopardy, she had no choice but to turn back to reinforce the frontier.

00:30.500 --> 00:41.500
Before long, the aristocratic alliance marched upon the imperial city. Knowing well that no reinforcements would come, you could only appoint Xie Xuan as Grand General to fight desperately to the end.

00:42.500 --> 00:49.500
Only then did Zhu Yuanzhi dispatch troops to defend the throne and quell the chaos, swiftly bringing the crisis under control and uniting with the clans to elevate the Second Prince, Sikong Xu, as the new Emperor.

00:51.320 --> 00:53.040
The 21st year of Longwu

00:53.320 --> 00:54.800
Sikong Xu ascended the throne

00:54.880 --> 00:56.160
Changed era name to Changning

00:56.320 --> 00:58.200
Appointed Zhu Yuanzhi as Grand General

00:58.400 --> 01:00.400
Commander of all military affairs

01:00.520 --> 01:03.080
May enter court without bowing, addressed without name

01:03.160 --> 01:04.640
May enter court with sword and shoes

01:04.760 --> 01:06.680
Granted the nine bestowments and yellow battle-axe

01:06.800 --> 01:09.800
Opened a government office equal to the Three Excellencies

01:21.000 --> 01:31.000
Three years later, Retired Emperor Sikong Yao 'succumbed to illness', prompting widespread rumors in the ranks. One autumn night of that same year, while the soldiers slept soundly, Zhu Yuanzhi's subordinates draped him in the imperial yellow robe...

01:31.500 --> 01:36.500
Upon awakening, Zhu Yuanzhi sighed ruefully: 'You fellows have truly placed me in a bitter bind.'
